  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "APN comes from the county parcel layer at 940 Main St, the address on the city's Major Development Projects page. The city project page gives no APN, so the site may include other parcels.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001167"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Biological Resource Evaluation (WRA, September 2025, revised January 2026) describes one building with 52 affordable units for households up to 60% AMI on APN 064-272-100, about 2 acres near 940 Main Street, east of Highway 1 between Poplar and Metzgar Streets. It was prepared to support a Half Moon Bay Coastal Development Permit application. The occupied residence at 940 Main Street stays in place because of its historic significance. The city project page describes three separate three-story buildings.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003465"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A County of San Mateo Department of Housing presentation lists Metzgar Street Apartments in pre-development: 51 affordable rental homes in Half Moon Bay, 13 set aside for agricultural workers. The city page and the biological report each show 52 units.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003466"
      ]
    }
  ],
